BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pitru Paksha begins / पितृ पक्ष आरंभ
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270916
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270917
DTSTAMP:20261103T045158Z
UID:pitru_paksha_start-2027-09-16@dharmasetu
CATEGORIES:ancestral\,festivals
DESCRIPTION:Why: set aside days so remembrance is not left to chance — fo
 od\, water and name offered with care.\n\nStory: Pitru Paksha opens after 
 Bhadrapada Purnima — a fortnight of shraddha for ancestors\, closing on 
 Sarvapitri Amavasya.\nSource: Garuda Purana\; Shraddha Kalpa traditions\nW
 hy: set aside days so remembrance is not left to chance — food\, water a
 nd name offered with care.\nModern angle: Structured mourning and remembra
 nce support grief processing\; cultural/psychological (see Worden / contin
 uing-bonds literature).\nEvidence: Plausible\nLink: https://pubmed.ncbi.nl
 m.nih.gov/20680363/\nMore: https://saumya-sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/revi
 ew/reasoning.html#shraddha-remembrance\nLocation basis: New Delhi. City-sp
 ecific timing coming later.
LOCATION:New Delhi\, India (reference)
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://saumya-sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/review/calendar.html#65b
 dddf8f1d44a71
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sarvapitri Amavasya / सर्वपित्नी अमाव
 स्या
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270929
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270930
DTSTAMP:20261103T045158Z
UID:sarvapitri-2027-09-30@dharmasetu
CATEGORIES:ancestral\,purnima-amavasya\,festivals
DESCRIPTION:Why: a safety-net day of remembrance so no lineage is left unn
 amed.\n\nStory: Sarvapitri Amavasya closes Pitru Paksha — the day for al
 l ancestors\, especially when individual tithi days were missed.\nSource: 
 Garuda Purana\; Shraddha manuals\nWhy: a safety-net day of remembrance so 
 no lineage is left unnamed.\nModern angle: Inclusive memorial day\; cultur
 al/psychological grief support.\nEvidence: Cultural/psychological\nMore: h
 ttps://saumya-sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/review/reasoning.html#shraddh
 a-remembrance\nLocation basis: New Delhi. City-specific timing coming late
 r.
LOCATION:New Delhi\, India (reference)
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://saumya-sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/review/calendar.html#ea0
 c668666d641be
END:VEVENT
